        "original_id": "ab120498-0bf9-53c5-9c96-72687b87d820",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius, Žemaitė\n- Products: Tautiška giesmė, Lithuanian National Anthem\n- Events: Lithuanian National Revival\n- Concepts: Lithuania, Lithuanian state, Lithuanian people\n\nFacts:\n- Vincas Kudirka was a Lithuanian poet and physician who lived from 31 December 1858 to 16 November 1899.\n- Vincas Kudirka was the author of both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian national anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė.\"\n- Tautiška giesmė is the national anthem of Lithuania.\n- Tautiška giesmė is also known by its opening words, \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų,\" and as \"Lietuvos himnas.\"\n- The fifty-word poem of Tautiška giesmė condensed Vincas Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\n- Vincas Kudirka and Jonas Basanavičius were among the most active participants in the Lithuanian National Revival.\n- Žemaitė, who was born to impoverished gentry, became one of the major participants in the Lithuanian National Revival.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
